c) Students present their spoken content by selecting and using target vocabulary and language structures similar and/or appropriate to those presented in the model/example considering their age, language level, context, style, and type of discourse for prepared and/or unprepared speaking situations.
d) Students convey relevant explicit, implicit, and/or complex messages related to the current content clearly in context to the listeners by using appropriate material and body language in prepared and/or unprepared speaking situations.
e) Students convey their messages about the current content clearly to the listeners by incorporating all the necessary semantic elements in prepared and/or unprepared speaking situations.', null, 'ENG.12.2', 'OGRENME_CIKTISI', 622, 631, null),
  ('52e869fc-61f7-5eff-9c8f-d345ba1c90cd', '4241cd0f-f778-52b3-a364-6d17d325fe96', 12, 'ING', 'ENG.12.2.S5', 'Students can reconstruct the information about ''''personal life and well-being with providing personal well-being through social health; providing personal well-being with economic stability (fashion addicts, shopaholics)'''' when communicating with others.', 'a) Students use the same or similar information presented in the current content in verbal or written forms in different contexts by reorganising it meaningfully, accurately, effectively, efficiently, functionally, and individually as required.
